@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] logging-trusted-origin
Origin identity and source routing MUST derive from trusted journal fields or
module-owned inputs, never fields in application messages. Restricted audit data
MUST require an explicit source selection on every destination.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] logging-independent-delivery
Exporters MUST run independently of application and VM lifetimes. Persistent
queues MUST have explicit bounds and destination failures MUST NOT stop guests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] logging-chunked-input-routes
The journal reader MUST keep at most eight conditional routes per input,
chunking the selected source surface across systemd input shards with distinct
cursor databases; tail inputs route only their own source. Fluent Bit 5.0.x
YAML parsing rejects larger per-input route lists at load time.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] logging-runtime-credentials
Destination secrets MUST be read from private runtime files, never embedded in
store configuration or command arguments. Diagnostic errors MUST use fixed text
without remote response bodies or rendered configuration.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] logging-sdk-health-closed
SDK health gauges MUST derive service identity from trusted journal units and
require that service's reviewed observability_health event. Only the four reviewed
trace health fields and trusted numeric event timestamp may become metrics:
availability is zero or one; pending,
queue drops and export failures are nonnegative finite integers. Other metadata
MUST NOT become metric values or labels. Host and unit labels MUST come from
module identity and trusted journal fields, preserving separate producers.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;deployment] logging-sdk-health-loopback
Fleet telemetry with logging MUST expose numeric application metrics on a distinct
loopback-only Prometheus exporter with an explicit queue budget. Numeric projection
MUST preserve original application log sources and routes; a metrics-only reader
MAY admit reviewed numeric records but MUST NOT export their application payloads.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] logging-runtime-projection
Application runtime gauges MUST use a matching trusted application unit and
catalogued runtime_metrics event; a metrics.summary payload from an application
unit MUST NOT be projected. Only the trusted operations collector unit MAY use the
closed metrics.summary shape. Numeric projection
MUST preserve the source log and attach only module/journal identity labels.
Runtime freshness MUST derive from the native journal timestamp, never payload
metadata or the time of a later scrape.
